      "title": "Here's a sample snapshot of the highlights from your four years as aWashington Fellow",
      "description": "Join the Fellows Program | Washington and Jefferson College Skip to content About Our Story Our Campus Centers for Leadership Offices & Departments Office of the President Cabinet Board of Trustees Campus Map Parents News Events Campus Store Give MyW&J Admissions & Aid First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Early Start Program Connect With A Counselor How To Apply Schedule A Visit Why W&J? Financial Aid & Scholarships Tuition & Fees For School Counselors Visit Campus Sep 26 Discovery Day at W&J 9:30 am - 1:30 pm More Events Academics Academics Majors and Minors Graduate Program in Professional Writing Master of Arts in Teaching Summer Program Beyond the Classroom Clark Family Library Faculty Support Our student-centered curriculum emphasizes professional readiness and intellectual curiosity. Explore Academics Student Life Student Life Residential Life & Dining Student Activities & Organizations First Year Experience The Magellan Project Washington Fellows Program Campus & Public Safety Disability Support Services Center for Career Advising and Networking Student Counseling Center International Student Initiatives Diversity & Leadership Initiatives Student Life Team Athletics Athletics GoPresidents.com Recruits Faculty & Staff Mentor Program Part of our holistic, leadership-focused experience, men's and women's sports challenge student-athletes to excel. Explore Athletics Alumni Alumni Jay Connected Volunteer Alumni events Ways to Give W&J Magazine Once a President, always a President. Your continued leadership helps current and future students realize their potential. Join the Alumni Community Search Admissions & Aid First-Year Students Transfer Students International Admission Accepted Students Early Start Program Connect with a Counselor How to Apply Schedule a Visit Why W&J Financial Aid & Scholarships Tuition & Fees For School Counselors Admission Events Academics Academics Majors & Minors Graduate Program in Professional Writing Master of Arts in Teaching Summer Program Beyond the Classroom Clark Family Library Faculty Support Student Life Student Life Residential Life & Dining Student Activities & Organizations First Year Experience The Magellan Project Washington Fellows Program Campus & Public Safety Disability Support Services Center for Career Advising and Networking Student Counseling Center International Student Services Diversity & Leadership Initiatives Student Life Team Athletics Athletics GoPresidents.com Recruits Faculty & Staff Mentor Program Alumni Alumni Jay Connected W&J Magazine Volunteer Alumni events Ways to Give About Our Story Our Campus Centers for Leadership Offices & Departments Office of the President Cabinet Board of Trustees Campus Map Parents News Events Campus Store Give MyW&J Campus Map Offices & Departments Emergency Contact Careers Privacy Policy Title IX Site Map Facebook Twitter Instagram 888-W-AND-JAY Contact WJ 60 S Lincoln St.,\nWashington, PA 15301 Search Admissions & Aid First-Year Students Transfer Students International Admission Accepted Students Early Start Program Connect with a Counselor How to Apply Schedule a Visit Why W&J Financial Aid & Scholarships Tuition & Fees For School Counselors Admission Events Academics Academics Majors & Minors Graduate Program in Professional Writing Master of Arts in Teaching Summer Program Beyond the Classroom Clark Family Library Faculty Support Student Life Student Life Residential Life & Dining Student Activities & Organizations First Year Experience The Magellan Project Washington Fellows Program Campus & Public Safety Disability Support Services Center for Career Advising and Networking Student Counseling Center International Student Services Diversity & Leadership Initiatives Student Life Team Athletics Athletics GoPresidents.com Recruits Faculty & Staff Mentor Program Alumni Alumni Jay Connected W&J Magazine Volunteer Alumni events Ways to Give About Our Story Our Campus Centers for Leadership Offices & Departments Office of the President Cabinet Board of Trustees Campus Map Parents News Events Campus Store Give MyW&J Campus Map Offices & Departments Emergency Contact Careers Privacy Policy Title IX Site Map Facebook Twitter Instagram 888-W-AND-JAY Contact WJ 60 S Lincoln St.,\nWashington, PA 15301 Search Plan a Visit (opens in new tab) Request Information (opens in new tab) Apply Now Home / Student Life / Washington Fellows Program Share on Facebook 𝕏 Share on X Share on Linkedin Share on WhatsApp Share on Email Share on Print The Washington Fellows is more than just your typical honors program. When you receive an invitation to the program during your senior year of high school, you'll have access to an established network of professionals who have graduated from the program, get hands-on experience with unique learning opportunities, and create long-lasting connections with your peers through this invaluable experience throughout your four years at W&J College. Explore all W&J Clubs Join the W&J Clubs Community We are on a MISSION at W&J. The Washington Fellows program seeks to provide additional opportunities for growth to students who have demonstrated a standard of academic and personal excellence. With a focus toward professional readiness, it is the mission of the program to graduate members who commit to living a life of impact. Here's a sample snapshot of the highlights from your four years as a Washington Fellow Each year has a unique Impact focus area (as noted below) First Year INTERNAL Symposia & Impact Groups Sophomore Year CAMPUS Leadership Junior Year COMMUNITY Service Senior Year LIFE Reflection & Coining Ceremony Expectations of a First Year Fellow Be an engaged member of your impact group Impact reflections (written reflection survey/check in) Report out in November Impact Groups Student led working groups charged with designing opportunities for the Fellows at large with emphasis on our tenants of service and leadership. Initiatives born out of the social and service groups > Impact Groups Membership Makeup Impact Leader (Student) First Year Fellows (assigned) Upper-class Fellows (optional, but encouraged) Benefits Capitalizes on internal talent and leadership > Impact Leaders cohort of talented, passionate students for each area (Impact Group) We can do more together! Animal Care Blood Drive Brother's Brother Campus Spirit Commuter Community Fellows Ball Food Insecurity Party with the Presidents Picnics with the Fellows Political Action PrezPantry PrezThon Service Experiences Social Opportunities Symposia TomTalks Women's Leadership Men's Development Mental Health Advocacy Student Newsletter Communications Team Fellows Events Lectures, days of service, leadership training, diversity training, and much more! Other Helpful Links Campus & Public Safety Career Advising & Networking Community Standards Club & Intramural Sports Diversity & Leadership Initiatives Fraternity & Sorority Life Crabtree Center for Student Wellbeing Community Engagement Magellan Project Future Students Academics Student Life Athletics Alumni Virtual Tour About W&J Parents News Events Give Campus Store Campus Map Offices & Departments Emergency Contact Careers Privacy Policy Title IX Site Map Get in Touch 888-W-AND-JAY Contact W&J 60 S Lincoln St., Washington, PA 15301 © 2026 Washington & Jefferson College. All Rights Reserved. Subscribe to news . Unsubscribe ."
