e Program in Professional Writing Master of Arts in Teaching Summer Program Beyond the Classroom Clark Family Library Faculty Support Student Life Student Life Residential Life & Dining Student Activities & Organizations First Year Experience The Magellan Project Washington Fellows Program Campus & Public Safety Disability Support Services Center for Career Advising and Networking Student Counseling Center International Student Services Diversity & Leadership Initiatives Student Life Team Athletics Athletics GoPresidents.com Recruits Faculty & Staff Mentor Program Alumni Alumni Jay Connected W&J Magazine Volunteer Alumni events Ways to Give About Our Story Our Campus Centers for Leadership Offices & Departments Office of the President Cabinet Board of Trustees Campus Map Parents News Events Campus Store Give MyW&J Campus Map Offices & Departments Emergency Contact Careers Privacy Policy Title IX Site Map Facebook Twitter Instagram 888-W-AND-JAY Contact WJ 60 S Lincoln St.,\nWashington, PA 15301 Search Admissions & Aid First-Year Students Transfer Students International Admission Accepted Students Early Start Program Connect with a Counselor How to Apply Schedule a Visit Why W&J Financial Aid & Scholarships Tuition & Fees For School Counselors Admission Events Academics Academics Majors & Minors Graduate Program in Professional Writing Master of Arts in Teaching Summer Program Beyond the Classroom Clark Family Library Faculty Support Student Life Student Life Residential Life & Dining Student Activities & Organizations First Year Experience The Magellan Project Washington Fellows Program Campus & Public Safety Disability Support Services Center for Career Advising and Networking Student Counseling Center International Student Services Diversity & Leadership Initiatives Student Life Team Athletics Athletics GoPresidents.com Recruits Faculty & Staff Mentor Program Alumni Alumni Jay Connected W&J Magazine Volunteer Alumni events Ways to Give About Our Story Our Campus Centers for Leadership Offices & Departments Office of the President Cabinet Board of Trustees Campus Map Parents News Events Campus Store Give MyW&J Campus Map Offices & Departments Emergency Contact Careers Privacy Policy Title IX Site Map Facebook Twitter Instagram 888-W-AND-JAY Contact WJ 60 S Lincoln St.,\nWashington, PA 15301 Search Center for Career Advising and Networking Plan a Visit (opens in new tab) Request Information (opens in new tab) Apply Now Home / Student Life / Center for Career Advising and Networking Share on Facebook 𝕏 Share on X Share on Linkedin Share on WhatsApp Share on Email Share on Print Washington & Jefferson College is known for preparing students to excel in careers ranging from medicine and law to technology and the arts. We call this professional readiness – the result of a progressive set of experiences that begin when you first arrive on campus and continue throughout your four years of education. The Center for Career Advising and Networking (CCAN) will support you in discerning your interests, sharpening your skills, and pursuing your long-term dreams. We see every student as an emerging professional, capable of mastering interpersonal and technical competencies to ensure a career success. In addition, the Center for Career Advising and Networking offers a suite of online services that include Handshake, providing online access to full-time, part-time, internship, work-study, and summer job opportunities; and Focus2Career, a career exploration platform. Signature Experiences, Superior Career Outcomes W&J’s signature experiences will empower you to achieve learning outcomes that align with eight career competencies identified by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE), a professional association focused on market trends and the attributes most sought by top employers. Graduate Outcomes In the Center for Career Advising and Networking, we regularly hear feedback from employers about our talented and prepared graduates. When you're a graduate of W&J College, you're a competitive candidate for employment and graduate study. 100% of students complete an internship or other professional experience while at W&J. Recruit W&J Students and Alumni If you're looking for the best new talent and graduates who are well prepared for the opportunities you have, you'll find the best candidates come from W&J College. Register with us to post your full-time, part-time, internship, seasonal, or freelance opportunities. Once you register, the Center for Career Advising and Networking will review your registration. After you're approved, you can start connecting with our students. Handshake Employer Registration The CCAN team is also available to collaborate on creative enhancements to your recruitment process. This includes, but is not limited to: campus branding opportunities, participation in career and internship fairs, and interacting with students in and out of the classroom. For more information, connect with us via email: ccan@washjeff.edu . We look forward to meeting you! More Resources See our MyW&J page for more information, resources, and links. Our Story Office of the President Elizabeth MacLeod Walls, Ph.D. Bio Title IX Coordinator & Compliance Human Resources Strategic Plan Board of Trustees Cabinet Offices And Departments Our Campus Our Buildings Campus Updates Campus Store Olin Fine Arts Center College Theatre Productions WNJR Radio Pittsburgh Connection Washington County Centers for Leadership Center for Career Advising and Networking Ignite Business Incubator Center for Energy and the Built Environment Sustainability At W&J Community Connection Statements of Solidarity President’s Perks Community Partners Program Consumer Information Privacy Policy Student Financial Aid Information Health, Safety and Security GDPR Statement Schedule a Visit Request Information Apply Today Other Helpful Links Campus & Public Safety Career Advising & Networking Community Standards Club & Intramural Sports Diversity & Leadership Initiatives Fraternity & Sorority Life Crabtree Center for Student Wellbeing Community Engagement Magellan Project Future Students Academics Student Life Athletics Alumni Virtual Tour About W&J Parents News Events Give Campus Store Campus Map Offices & Departments Emergency Contact Careers Privacy Policy Title IX Site Map Get in Touch 888-W-AND-JAY Contact W&J 60 S Lincoln St., Washington, PA 15301 © 2026 Washington & Jefferson College. All Rights Reserved. Subscribe to news . Unsubscribe ."
